From 1d4fe51b10d756044cd7cfa4b951664b142678f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:26:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 067/110] media: sprd: add SC7730 camera capture driver (DCAM +
 CSI-2)

The Spreadtrum SC7730 (and SC8830 "shark") captures camera data through
a Synopsys DesignWare CSI-2 host (v1.03) with two D-PHYs (A: 2 lanes,
C: 1 lane) feeding the DCAM engine. This driver uses DCAM path 1 with
the scaler bypassed as a plain receiver for sensors that have their
own ISP and deliver YUV422.

Path 1 writes a Y plane and an interleaved CbCr plane (NV16, U first
with little-endian UV order). There is no line pitch register, so lines
are packed and the CbCr plane starts at width * height. Frame addresses
are shadowed: the address for the next frame is programmed at the
path's start of frame and latched at the following one by auto copy,
as the vendor driver does; a scratch buffer absorbs frames when user
space has nothing queued. A missing PATH1_DONE between two SOFs puts
the buffer back in the queue.

The driver is MC-centric (one video node, one sink pad, a link to each
bound sensor; the first one bound is enabled). It programs the D-PHY
from the sensor's link frequency with the vendor's hsfreqrange/settle
table, provides the sensor master clock (24 MHz from the MM clock
block) and handles the MM power domain through runtime PM. MM AHB, the
MM clock registers and AON APB are shared with other blocks and mapped
without claiming them.

Tested on the Samsung Galaxy Tab E 9.6 (SM-T560) with the front
SR200PC20M on D-PHY C: 640x480, 800x600 and 1600x1200 stream without
errors, frame timing even, format mismatches with the sensor fail with
EPIPE, the MM domain is off when idle.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
